==== From OEM firmware with web upload installation ====

OpenWrt can be installed from OEM/factory using the [[:docs:guide-quick-start:factory_installation|standard firmware update method]].

**Notes:** 
  * You do not need to factory reset the router if it has been previously configured, but the flash of openwrt*-factory.bin will reset configuration.
  * If in factory reset state, disconnect WAN cable and bypass netgear's genie first-time install to access the firmware update page.
  * When flashing from OEM to *-factory.bin, the router may warn you that this firmware is an older version than currently installed: it is ok to proceed.
  * Flash and reboot takes about 3 minutes
//Confirmed upgrade from factory v1.1.0.28_1.0.1 to OpenWrt 22.03.5//

